  "question": {
    "text": "Let the points of intersections of the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are the mid points of the sides of a triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABC</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABC</mi></math> is"
  },
